      "message": "PFD is tricky in terms of dup/closing... Checked that the generated AIDL with ParcelFileDescriptor will do:\nif (pfd !\u003d null) {\n  _data.writeInt(1);\n  pfd.writeToParcel(_data);\n}\n\npfd.writeToParcel essentially does:\nwriteInt(0);\nwriteFileDescriptor(mFd);\n\nSo compared to the original writeRawFileDescriptor(fd) that is generated by using FileDescriptor, this should be equivalent (writeFileDescriptor updates the \"native size\" of the Parcel but does the same thing as writeRawFileDescriptor).\n",
